hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16406","He said: Abd al-Samad and Surayj said: Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Badr narrated to us that Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali narrated to him that his father Ali ibn Shayban narrated to him that he went out as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: So we prayed behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he glanced with the corner of his eye at a man who did not straighten his back in bowing and prostration, and when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished he said: O company of Muslims, there is no prayer for one who does not straighten his back in bowing and prostration. He said: And he saw a man praying alone behind the row, so he stood until the man finished, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Repeat your prayer, for there is no prayer for a lone man behind the row. Abd al-Samad said: Alone behind the row. Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Abu Abdullah al-Shaqari narrated to me, he said: Amr ibn Jabir narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Badr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali ibn Shayban, from his father, and he mentioned it. Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Utba informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Badr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali ibn Shayban al-Suhaymi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, and he mentioned it."
"16407","He said: Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn Badr narrated to me, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father Talq ibn Ali, he said: He said: A scorpion stung me in the presence of the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he performed ruqya for me and wiped it."
